Map decimal m3u track numbers to libgme's 0-based tracks.

Decimal track numbers in m3u playlists (NSF,01) are 1-based; hexadecimal ones
(NSF,$00) are 0-based. The vendored kode54 snapshot commented out the
decimal adjustment that blargg's libgme applies, so every decimal entry
played the following song and the last entry failed with "invalid track in
m3u playlist". Restore the upstream rule: subtract one for decimal tracks
unless the type uses 0-based decimal numbering (flags_ & 0x02, e.g. KSS),
and reject the resulting -1 of a decimal track 0 as an invalid track.

Upstream: generic bug, suitable for xbmc/audiodecoder.gme (and kode54's
Game_Music_Emu).

--- a/lib/Game_Music_Emu/gme/Gme_File.cpp
+++ b/lib/Game_Music_Emu/gme/Gme_File.cpp
@@ -102,11 +102,11 @@
 		if ( e.track >= 0 )
 		{
 			*track_io = e.track;
-			// TODO: really needs to be removed?
-			//if ( !(type_->flags_ & 0x02) )
-			//  *track_io -= e.decimal_track;
+			// Decimal m3u tracks are 1-based unless the type says otherwise.
+			if ( !(type_->flags_ & 0x02) )
+				*track_io -= e.decimal_track;
 		}
-		if ( *track_io >= raw_track_count_ )
+		if ( (unsigned) *track_io >= (unsigned) raw_track_count_ )
 			return BLARGG_ERR( BLARGG_ERR_FILE_CORRUPT, "invalid track in m3u playlist" );
 	}
 	else
